From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:21:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [libpng] BUILD.gn: use the portable filters on ppc64

pngpriv.h defines PNG_POWERPC_VSX_OPT=2 whenever __PPC64__, __ALTIVEC__
and __VSX__ are defined, which clang does by default for ppc64le. Then
png_read_filter_row() references png_init_filter_functions_vsx() from
powerpc/powerpc_init.c, which BUILD.gn never compiles, and every binary
linking Skia fails:

  pngrutil.c: undefined reference to `png_init_filter_functions_vsx'

Define PNG_POWERPC_VSX_OPT=0 on ppc64 (the portable C filters, as for
x86 here). Compiling powerpc/*.c instead would enable libpng's VSX
filters; left for later, measured against the portable path.

Class: upstreamable fix (to flutter's libpng BUILD.gn).
---
 BUILD.gn | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engine/src/flutter/third_party/libpng/BUILD.gn b/engine/src/flutter/third_party/libpng/BUILD.gn
index 3448491..e4d8c94 100644
--- a/engine/src/flutter/third_party/libpng/BUILD.gn
+++ b/engine/src/flutter/third_party/libpng/BUILD.gn
@@ -43,6 +43,15 @@ source_set("libpng") {
     cflags_c += [ "-Wno-sign-compare" ]
   }
 
+  if (current_cpu == "ppc64") {
+    # pngpriv.h turns on PNG_POWERPC_VSX_OPT=2 whenever the compiler defines
+    # __PPC64__/__ALTIVEC__/__VSX__ (clang does by default on ppc64le), which
+    # makes png_read_filter_row() call png_init_filter_functions_vsx() from
+    # powerpc/powerpc_init.c -- a file this build does not compile. Use the
+    # portable filters, as on every other non-ARM CPU here.
+    defines += [ "PNG_POWERPC_VSX_OPT=0" ]
+  }
+
   if (is_win) {
     cflags_c += [ "-Wno-tautological-constant-out-of-range-compare" ]
   }
